      &nbsp;/&nbsp; <a href="tours.html">Destinations</a> &nbsp;/&nbsp;
      Chongqing</span><h1>Chongqing <span class="zh"
      style="font-family:var(--font-zh);font-size:0.65em;color:var(--gold);">重庆</span></h1><p>Chongqing
      is China's mountain city of fog and fire — a neon-lit metropolis stacked
      on steep hills where the Yangtze and Jialing rivers meet, and the
      birthplace of fiery hotpot.</p></div></section>
  - label: Why visit Chongqing?
    html: >
      <section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="split"><div
      class="split-media reveal"><img src="assets/img/dest-chongqing.jpg"
      alt="Chongqing" /><div class="seal-stamp"
      aria-hidden="true">重<br/>庆</div></div><div class="split-copy reveal
      reveal-d1"><span class="eyebrow">Mountain City</span><h2
      class="display-h2">Why visit Chongqing?</h2><p>Chongqing is a city that
      defies gravity — roads loop over rooftops, a monorail flies straight
      through a residential tower, and Hongya Cave's golden stilted houses glow
      above the river at night. With 30 million residents it is China's largest
      municipality, yet its soul lives in hillside alleys, riverside teahouses
      and steaming hotpot pots shared late into the night.</p><p>Few cities in
      China blend futuristic skyline, raw street energy and World Heritage
      landscapes within a day trip's reach. Add famously warm-hearted locals and
      the country's boldest cuisine, and you get one of China's most
      unforgettable urban adventures.</p></div></div></div></section>
