  - label: Taste of the Mountain City
    html: >
      <section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="split"><div
      class="split-copy reveal"><span class="eyebrow">Food Capital</span><h2
      class="display-h2">Taste of the Mountain City</h2><p>Chongqing is the
      birthplace of Chinese hotpot — a bubbling beef-tallow broth divided into
      nine grids, each simmering at its own heat. Dinner here is theatre: order
      a tower of sliced beef, tripe and lotus root, dunk, dip in garlic oil, and
      cool down with sour plum juice.</p><p>Beyond hotpot, the city's street
      food scene rewards every detour. Our guides take you to the back-alley
      institutions locals actually queue for — not the tourist traps.</p><ul
      class="tour-highlights"
      style="grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:10px;"><li><strong>Xiaomian</strong>
      — the legendary spicy small noodles locals eat for
      breakfast</li><li><strong>Suanlafen</strong> — hot-and-sour glass noodles
      with crispy peas</li><li><strong>Jiangtuan fish</strong> — Yangtze river
      fish hotpot, milder and deeply savoury</li><li><strong>Ciqikou
      mahua</strong> — hand-twisted fried dough crisps in the old
      town</li></ul></div><div class="split-media reveal reveal-d1"><img
      src="assets/img/chongqing-hotpot.jpg" alt="Chongqing nine-grid hotpot"
      /><div class="seal-stamp"
      aria-hidden="true">火<br/>锅</div></div></div></div></section>
